\tag{fdip}
\title{The blocking step and its towers}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{The nested residue classes of \ref{fdip-0099} separate fluctuations
inside a block from the field constant on that block. The marginal
calculation of \ref{fdip-000D} determines how these two parts enter the
precision of the block field. When can the coarser precision be read by
compression, and which choices remain compatible through every depth?}

